,"cmd-df7a66f079df4f73","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. usb-storage was blocked immediately and remained blocked after a directly observed reboot, while the OS release and kernel were preserved. The restart protocol coherently shows a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot, changed boot identity, running recovered system, read-write root filesystem, successful modules-load service, and persistent task configuration.","limitations":["No physical USB mass-storage hot-plug test was captured; enforcement was instead demonstrated through direct modprobe attempts before and after reboot. No application-specific data service or multi-node cluster was part of the managed topology, so restart recovery evidence is limited to system health, root-filesystem availability, module service state, and task configuration."]}
